==[[Toon of the Week]] Quests==
{{TOTWQuests|Visit the [[Art Gallery]] [[floor]] 3 times.|Complete a [[machine]] debuffed by {{CI|Twisted Brusha|name=true}}.|Complete 20 machine buffs using '''{{AI|Brusha|name=true}}.}}

===Rewards===
*1 Quest completed: {{AT|Brusha Fan}} [[Title]]
*2 Quests completed: {{SI|Golden Brusha!|name=true}} [[Sticker]]
*3 Quests completed: {{Skin|Golden Bristles|toon=Brusha}} [[Skin]]

===Strategies===
*For the first Quest, you should just play normally, progressing through [[Floors]]. However, once you reach a high Floor like Floor 15, you should restart a run, as those early-run Floors spawn less the higher you go.
*For the second Quest, just keep playing until you see {{CI|Twisted Brusha|name=true}} on your Floor. Then, just wait for her to vandalize a [[Machine]] and do it. It is recommended to play with friends/alone so this opportunity isn't stolen by others.
*For the third Quest, play as Brusha and just repeatedly paint Machines you see.

==Requirement Strategies==
*For the first requirement, focus on picking up [[Research Capsules]] and extracting [[Machines]]. The Machine and Capsule count increases the further you descend, so you can earn more {{II|Ichor|name=true}}.
*For the second requirement, have a Distractor Toon bring {{CI|Twisted Brusha|name=true}} to the [[Elevator]] to you so you can get aggro. Playing as {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} also helps getting Research faster because of his Passive Ability. This will be easier Since Twisted Brusha is a {{Type|Common}} Twisted, she has a higher chance of appearing during the [[Floors]], and you only need 25% research to be able to obtain Brusha.

==Strategies==
Brusha is rather well-rounded, having 4{{Star}} [[Skill Check]] at the cost of lower [[Stealth]], with a specialization in extraction and support thanks to her [[Ability]], {{AI|Brusha|name=true}}.

'''Artistic Inspiration''' works somewhat like a fusion of other Skill Check and Extraction Speed boosts, granting a +15% Skill Check chance boost and a +25% Extraction Speed boost to any [[Toons]] who extract from a painted [[Machine]]. This is quite useful—it can help the extraction of Toons with low Extraction Speed, or it can further boost those with already high extraction. The Extraction Speed boost is potent enough that it can roughly add a Star worth to any Toon, possibly even being more than a Star. Unlike other non-[[Trinket]] sources, this boost is infinite and applied to Machines themselves, which can be very beneficial as it means players can't waste it if they get spotted by a [[Twisted]] or get off the Machine to fulfill a different task. If Brusha only ever extracts buffed Machines, she has an average completion time the ''near'' equivalent of a Toon with 4 Stars in Skill Check and 5 Stars in Extraction Speed.

Since her Ability passively highlights Machines nearby with a white highlight and white paintbrush icon, even through walls, she may be able to find them a bit more quickly than other Toons, especially ones in blind spots. She can also use her Ability to mark certain Machines as they'll be marked with an occasional pink highlight and orange paintbrush icon when buffed/painted, no matter how far away she is; the latter of which specifically is shown to all players, even through walls. These icons could for example be used to mark a primed/99% filled Machine. Do note that the buff does not have any effect on Treadmill Machines, as they only utilize [[Movement Speed]] and [[Stamina]], with Skill Checks having a set frequency irrespective of chance; you you can still mark them so others know where they are, particularly those that excel with Treadmill Machines.

There are a few things you should note when it comes to the painting minigame. For one, check your surroundings before initiating it, as you could get caught off guard while painting. Moving too far away from the Machine you're attempting to buff will cancel the minigame and reset your cooldown to 0, making your Ability immediately ready again. {{TI|Peppermint Icing|name=true}} activates when the minigame is initiated, not when you buff a Machine; with this in mind you could activate the minigame and cancel it multiple times back to back, in order to regenerate a large amount of Stamina, since the cooldown is reset if you don’t buff a Machine. You can also run by a Machine while being chased by a Twisted, and then initiate the minigame to regain Stamina in order to escape more easily, or even divert Twisteds away from teammates. When you complete the minigame and buff a Machine, {{TI|Party Popper|name=true}} will activate as if you began extracting a Machine, which could prove useful as you can know if there's any Twisteds nearby who could interrupt extracting, or block a path to a different Machine you plan to buff next.

Brusha can really shine when extracting with another Toon on a Duo Machine, as her Ability's boost will be applied to both herself and her teammate. Even if she herself doesn't extract from a buffed Duo Machine, she can still really heat up the extraction of two other players on one. She can also be really good when paired up with {{CI|Shelly|name=true}}. A painted Machine's 25% boost stacks with Shelly's 75% boost from {{AI|Shelly|name=true}}, totaling to a whopping 118.8%, meaning a team would practically have an infinite supply of {{II|Instructions|name=false}} and more. Plus, both of their boosts work pretty well with each other's Stat spreads.

Artistic Inspiration's biggest weakness is when {{CI|Twisted Brusha|name=true}} and/or {{CI|Twisted Tisha|name=true}} is on the [[Floor]]. Both of the aforementioned Twisteds can change painted Machines into vandalized or normal states respectively, therefore removing the buff. On the other hand, you are able to simply re-paint them, though it can be inconvenient. You can however disrupt their special abilities by grabbing their attention, or have a distractor to maintain the painted Machines. These Twisteds are both {{Type|Common}}, meaning they'll show up more on early Floors rather than later, so in the long term this shouldn't be too big of an issue.

Brusha can be a good Toon to have on the team if you plan on spawning {{CI|Twisted Dyle|name=true}}, as she can very easily buff Machines, therefore allowing [[Dyle's Floor]] to be completed faster. Her higher Skill Check makes her extract at an above average pace, while also reducing the risk of failing Skill Checks. The +50 Stamina capacity gained from completing the Floor is useful, as Brusha can afford to run more often while scouting for and buffing Machines, or running away from Twisteds (something she has more risk of due to her Stealth).

Any [[Items]] can help make Brusha better at her tasks, extraction related Items work with her above average extraction Stats, and stack with her painted Machine boosts. Mobility Items can allow her to move quickly and easily navigate a Floor, or even protect teammates with her lower Stealth. Healing Items might be slightly more useful considering she has lower Stealth, which results in a higher likelihood of being chased by Twisteds, and thus more potential of losing {{Heart}}.

Overall, Brusha is quite well-rounded, with a versatile Ability that can support others and boost herself. She can be pretty good in solo runs since she'll always boost Machines she herself will extract. It’s recommended to be cautious as her average speed and lower Stealth can still make certain Twisteds particularly dangerous, or cause excess Stamina loss.

